          "properties": {},
          "scale": "md",
          "width": 1168,
          "height": 160,
          "note": "# Caution\n\nThe ML-KEM Encapsulate process is probabilistic: it injects fresh internal randomness on every run, producing a completely unique `Shared Key` and `Ciphertext` each time, even with the same public key. \n\nThis dynamically generated secret cannot be statically predicted; only a recipient holding the corresponding `Secret Key` can process the `Ciphertext` via ML-KEM Decapsulate to accurately recover the matching `Shared Key` for that specific session.",
          "bg": "yellow"
        },
